      "quirks": [
        "Smith County marriage volumes 1857-1876 and 1875-1889 (FamilySearch volumes 007255720, 007255721) are 100% name-indexed and full-text searchable — a further search for an EARLIER marriage of the same bride (under any surname) is straightforward.",
        "Hill County probate case files 1853-1935 (volume 004820309) are full-text searchable but only ~3% name-indexed — keyword-search required for a father's estate naming Martha as an heir.",
        "Texas did not require statewide civil registration of births/deaths until 1903; pre-1903 events rely on church, cemetery, marriage, and probate records."
      ],
      "guide_markdown": "# Locality Guide: Hill County and Smith County, Texas (circa 1855-1890)\n\nSmith County marriage volumes 1857-1889 are fully indexed and full-text searchable — well suited to searching for an earlier marriage under a different surname. Hill County probate is full-text searchable but not name-indexed. No civil vital registration before 1903.",
